tasks.details:
Preferred location: Traefik middleware in compose.yml (no code change, applies to all responses)

Steps:
1. Add a Traefik headers middleware in compose.yml:
   ```yaml
   # In the proxy/traefik labels or a dynamic config file:
   traefik.http.middlewares.security-headers.headers.contentSecurityPolicy: >-
     default-src 'self';
     script-src 'self';
     style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
     img-src 'self' data: https:;
     connect-src 'self' https://sentry.io;
     font-src 'self';
     frame-ancestors 'none';
     base-uri 'self';
     form-action 'self'
   traefik.http.middlewares.security-headers.headers.xFrameOptions: DENY
   traefik.http.middlewares.security-headers.headers.xContentTypeOptions: nosniff
   traefik.http.middlewares.security-headers.headers.referrerPolicy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
   traefik.http.middlewares.security-headers.headers.permissionsPolicy: >-
     camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
   ```
2. Apply middleware to frontend router: `traefik.http.routers.frontend.middlewares=security-headers`
3. Do NOT apply CSP to the backend API router (would block Swagger UI and API responses)
4. Test with https://securityheaders.com after deploy
5. For local dev, add the same middleware to compose.override.yml frontend service

Note: 'unsafe-inline' in style-src is needed for Tailwind's runtime injection. If Tailwind moves to fully static CSS, this can be removed.

1. Add a `Disclaimer` component at `frontend/src/components/ui/Disclaimer.tsx`:
```tsx
interface IProps {
  children: React.ReactNode
  className?: string
}

function Disclaimer({ children, className }: Readonly<IProps>) {
  return (
    <div className={cn(
      "rounded-md border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50 px-4 py-3 text-xs text-rose-800",
      className
    )}>
      {children}
    </div>
  )
}

export default Disclaimer
```
   Use Tailwind's rose palette (closest to light wine) — `bg-rose-50 border-rose-200 text-rose-800`.

2. Replace all inline disclaimer `<p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">` patterns across calculators, mietpreisbremse, document translation, and property evaluation with `<Disclaimer>`.

3. Grep pattern to find all disclaimer text: `disclaimer` (the field name) and phrases like "verify with", "consult a", "not legal advice", "not financial advice".

4. Export from `frontend/src/components/ui/index.ts`.

5. No backend changes needed.
